##############################################################################
#  URFD G3 Terminal Options
#
#  Configures Icom Terminal/Access Point mode (G3 protocol).
#  One option per line.
#
#  Options:
#    address <ip>       Public IP for terminal route responder.
#                        Without it a terminal is told the address its packet
#                        came in at, and behind NAT (a private address) a
#                        terminal on the internet urfd's external IPv4
#                        ([IP Addresses], followed while urfd runs); set it to
#                        fix the address.
#    modules <modules>  Modules that accept terminal connections.
#                        Default: * (all modules)
#    alias <callsign>   Additional reflector callsign accepted from terminals
#                        (e.g. to accept both URFxxx and XLXxxx). Repeatable.
#
#  Examples:
#    address 203.0.113.1
#    modules BCD
#    alias XLX363
#
##############################################################################
#address 203.0.113.1
#modules BCD
#alias XLX363
